{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:9e2806192a3a120a","name":"Krayt Dragon","source":{"id":"source:reference-9e2806192a3a120a","title":"Krayt Dragon","revision":18950,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:01:44Z","sha256":"7fb724ebc7edd71088bccb79134bcfea35fdb44c2cf6d53c69e5cc2e2651e6ca","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18950","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Krayt%20Dragon&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-9e2806192a3a120a","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Krayt Dragon is a truly massive beast. This 100-meter-long desert titan lives among the endless dunes of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"},". A Krayt Dragon actually submerges itself in the shifting sands, and can use it's ten powerful limbs to swim through the dunes.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"}," natives rarely see a living Krayt Dragon, although the titanic bones of these creatures dot the landscape and are highly prized as building material or trade goods. The gigantic reptile prefers to lurk under the warm desert during the day, moving about at night as it slinks close to the surface of the sand. A Krayt Dragon attacks with its massive jaws or whiplike tail; its claws have evolved exclusively for locomotion. Krayt Dragons subsist on the largest prey, including herds of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Banthas"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Banthas"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dewbacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dewbacks"},". Anything that moves across a Krayt Dragon's field of vision is fair game, though.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Krayt Dragon Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["If a truly determined hunter were to penetrate the beast's armored hide and slay a Krayt Dragon, that hunter would be rewarded with an Emperor's ransom in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Krayt Dragon Pearls"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Krayt_Dragon_Pearls"},"- ordinary stones polished to priceless perfection in the dragon's stomach. A single such stone could fetch well over 100,000 credits. A Krayt Dragon contains 2d4+2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Krayt Dragon Pearls"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Krayt_Dragon_Pearls"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Krayt Dragons are always encountered singly- although it's possible to run into a Krayt Dragon that is in the middle of assaulting a herd of animals, adding to the danger as these panicked animals run for their lives. Too stupid to notice (and too tough to care) that they aren't edible, Krayt Dragons commonly attack ",{"tag":"a","children":["Landspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Landspeeders"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jawa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jawa","referenceId":"reference:0b0fb3f831db6b3c"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sandcrawlers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sandcrawlers"},", and other large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},". A Krayt Dragon's lair can sometimes be discerned by the \"melted\" remains of some ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," that sat a long time in the creature's stomach before it was spat up as being indigestible. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Enterprising and extremely foolhardy hunters sometimes stalk Krayt Dragons with massive firepower or on swoops, allowing them to make numerous hit-and-run attacks, in the hope of killing a Krayt Dragon and stealing the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Krayt Dragon Pearls"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Krayt_Dragon_Pearls"}," inside. Predictably, casualties on such ventures are high.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Krayt Dragon Statistics (CL 16)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal Desert ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 17\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +6; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", Tremorsense, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +14\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 16), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 30, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 399, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 15, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 80\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 10 Squares; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Powerful Charge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Powerful_Charge","referenceId":"reference:d7f59c39adb93fd7"},"\n"]},{"tag":